  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Inside the Heart was included in Slash, Paper Under The Knife at the Museum of Arts &amp; Design in New York City, and in the book Masters: Book Arts: Major Works by Leading Artists. Inside the Heart creates a visual space and invites the viewer to supply a narrative.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A dioramic art work consisting of 4 hand cut and hand painted interconnected paper frames with red tendrils through which two hands reach toward each other. It can be viewed as a tunnel book inside a specially constructed black display box with custon lighting that accents different parts of the art work, depending on the placement of the book in the box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unique book.</subfield>
